# .agents - AI Agent Capabilities & System Discovery Manifest
<!-- Advanced CSS Studio System Core Engine -->

## 1. System Identity
- Provider: Advanced CSS Studio Edge Engine
- Workbench: Adaptive CSS Workbench & Layout Engineering Suite
- Discovery Path: /etc/ai-agent-manifest.json
- Schema: 2026.10-v1

## 2. [file provider] Protocol & MIME Adjustments
- Protocol: css-studio-vfs://
- Mount Point: /studio-workspace
- Engine Features:
  - 60s Delayed Revocation on Blob Streams (mitigates Chromium race conditions)
  - Data URI Fallback for sandboxed iframes
  - Content-Disposition: attachment server streaming via /api/download/file
  - Clipboard buffer interceptor if disk write is rejected

### Standard MIME Pair Adjustments
- .css      : text/css; charset=utf-8 (attachment)
- .min.css  : text/css; charset=utf-8 (attachment)
- .txt      : text/plain; charset=utf-8 (attachment)
- .json     : application/json; charset=utf-8 (attachment)
- .agents   : text/markdown; charset=utf-8 (inline)
- .svg      : image/svg+xml; charset=utf-8 (inline)
- .html     : text/html; charset=utf-8 (attachment)

## 3. [api edge function and discovery in /etc]
- Edge Config: /etc/ai-agent-manifest.json
- Symlink: /etc/css-studio/agent.conf
- Endpoints:
  - POST /api/download/file (Attachment Stream with Content-Disposition)
  - GET  /api/preferences/desktop-delivery.txt (CORS TXT Delivery for Daemons & CLI)
  - POST /api/preferences/sync (Bi-directional State Sync)
  - POST /api/scan-legacy-css (Chromium Engine Scanner)
  - GET  /api/agents/discovery (Machine-parseable Discovery Spec)

## 4. CSS Linter @import Guidance
- Policy: @import cascaded waterfalls are prohibited in production bundles.
- DO NOT: Do not use @import inside stylesheets because it blocks parallel network downloads.
- WARN: Halts browser rendering until imported stylesheets are fully loaded (delaying FCP).
- TIP: Use HTML <link rel="stylesheet"> or combine into a single minified bundle.
